# Human Review Required

Use this rule before any article, calculator methodology, or financial explainer is considered final or publication-ready.

## Do

- Treat every agent-created or agent-edited article as requiring human review.
- Require human review of factual claims, formulas, assumptions, citations, SEO metadata, schema, internal links, and final wording.
- Keep draft status visible until the user explicitly approves publication.
- Ask for confirmation before moving content from `/drafts/` into live article paths or registering it in build, sitemap, search, or hubs.
- Flag high-risk items for the human reviewer: tax rules, thresholds, source freshness, ambiguous arithmetic, and policy interpretation.

## Do Not

- Do not mark an article final, published, approved, or legally/tax accurate on an agent's authority.
- Do not auto-publish drafts, add them to public navigation, or remove review markers without explicit user instruction.
- Do not resolve factual uncertainty by smoothing the prose.
- Do not hide unresolved verification work in comments, metadata, or omitted caveats.
